---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Hero from "../../components/Hero.astro";
import VpdCalculator from "../../components/VpdCalculator.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="VPD and Dew Point Calculator"
  description="Compute leaf VPD, night dew point setpoints, and the dew point of a room you already have, in Fahrenheit and Celsius, from the same Magnus equation behind our grow schedule."
>
  <Hero title="VPD and Dew Point Calculator" />

  <div style="max-width:var(--content-width);">
    <p class="calc-intro">
      Every figure in a day or night setpoint table comes from one equation and two choices.
      Enter your own numbers to build the same tables for your room. For why the day is steered by
      <a href="/glossary/vapor-pressure-deficit/">VPD</a> and the night by
      <a href="/glossary/dew-point/">dew point</a>, read
      <a href="/blog/vpd-by-day-dew-point-by-night/">VPD by day, dew point by night</a>.
    </p>

    <VpdCalculator />

    <p class="calc-footnote">
      The math is the <a href="/glossary/magnus-equation/">Magnus equation</a> for
      <a href="/glossary/saturation-vapor-pressure/">saturation vapor pressure</a>, run entirely in
      your browser. Temperatures are entered in Fahrenheit and shown in both units. Nothing you type
      leaves the page.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .calc-intro {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .calc-intro a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .calc-footnote {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .calc-footnote a {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
